 ],
 "literal": "The tall chariot with a curved handhold, adorned with ornaments, coming gracefully, / having stopped and rested on the mountain-like vast sand dunes, / if you stayed, would it be a fault? / So that the loneliness of this woman, whose waist is adorned with hanging leaf-garments, departs, / in that place where the curved backwater with swaying waves is surrounded by screw-pines / and sounds with a rushing noise, / in our small, good village fenced by the vast ocean.",
 "translation": "O Lord! If you stop your tall chariot, adorned with ornaments and fitted with a curved handhold, which comes gracefully, and rest on these mountain-like vast sand dunes, and stay with us, would it be a fault? It would dispel the loneliness of this girl who wears a low-hanging skirt of leaves, here in our small, beautiful village fenced by the vast ocean, where the curved backwater with swaying waves is surrounded by screw-pines and murmurs with a rushing sound.",
 "modern": "ஆபரணங்களால் அலங்கரிக்கப்பட்டு, அழகாக வரும் வளைந்த கொடுஞ்சியைக் கொண்ட பெரிய தேரை, மலை போன்ற உயர்ந்த மணல் மேட்டில் நிறுத்தி, இளைப்பாறி, நீங்கள் தங்கிச் சென்றால் அது குற்றமாகுமா? தழையாடையை உடுத்திய இவளுடைய தனிமைத் துயர் நீங்குமாறு, தாழை மரங்கள் சூழ்ந்த, அசையும் அலைகளைக் கொண்ட வளைந்த உப்பங்கழி 'இழு' என்று ஒலியெழுப்பும் இடத்திலுள்ள, பெரிய கடலை வேலியாகக் கொண்ட எங்களது சிறிய நல்ல ஊரில் நீங்கள் தங்குவது தவறோ?",
 "explanation": "The speaker is the heroine's friend (thōḻi), addressing the hero who has been visiting the heroine secretly by day. She gently suggests that he should stay in their village instead of returning home, hinting at a permanent union (marriage) rather than fleeting trysts. The poem is set in the Neytal (coastal) landscape, characterized by the vast ocean, sand dunes, screw-pines (tāḻai), and backwaters (kaḻi). The image of the chariot resting on the dunes reflects the desire for the hero to halt his journeys and settle down. The rushing sound of the backwater ('iḻumena') emphasizes the lively yet lonely atmosphere of the coastal village that awaits his presence.",
